  "articleBody": "Thinking about hiring a professional to put in a kitchen backsplash? It is easy to focus purely on tile colors and grout swatches, but the quality of the finished wall comes down to what happens behind the scenes. Before signing a contract, you want to know how the installer handles wall prep, uneven surfaces, and electrical safety.\n\nQuestions to Ask Before You Decide\n- Wall condition: Will they repair drywall dips, patches, or grease spots before applying adhesive? Large-format and mosaic tiles both reveal wavy drywall instantly.\n- Electrical layout: Do they shut off breaker circuits and adjust outlet boxes so plates sit flush against finished tile?\n- Expansion gaps: Do they plan for a flexible movement gap along the countertop edge, or do they mistakenly fill that joint with rigid grout?\n- Edging details: How will exposed runs finish? Ask about metal trim profiles or bullnose pieces so raw tile edges are not left bare.\n\nDecision Factor\nIf your kitchen has older plaster, sagging drywall, or outlets placed at irregular heights, you need a contractor with solid carpentry and drywall repair skills. HH Remodeling LLC handles full-scope finish work across Aurora, Denver, and Littleton, ensuring your walls are prepped level before any adhesive is spread. Call Abraham Becerra at 303-505-0866 to discuss your project.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
